# Code owners.
#
# The trailer guard is a guardrail on the assistant's own commit messages, and
# its `guard-self-test` CI job runs the acceptance matrix of the pull request it
# is checking. Without an owner on these paths, one pull request could weaken
# the predicate, weaken the matrix and edit the workflow together, pass its own
# weakened test, and go green. Requiring a named human review on exactly these
# three paths is what keeps the guard from validating itself.
#
# NOTE: a CODEOWNERS entry only binds once branch protection on the default
# branch has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. That toggle is an
# operator action in the repository settings, not something this file can do.

/scripts/check-no-ai-trailers.sh         @lfdesousa
/scripts/check-no-ai-trailers.test.sh    @lfdesousa
/.github/workflows/no-ai-trailers.yml    @lfdesousa
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @lfdesousa
